  "job_B3.2.34_20251003_114632": {
    "text": "Men \u00f0a leofestan, us gedafena\u00fe \u00e6rest \u00fe\u00e6t we gemunen & gereccen be Gode \u00e6lmihtigum, \u00fee geworhte\nEalle \u00fery, se f\u00e6der & se sunu & se haliga gast, w\u00e6ron \u00e6fre efenece & \u00e6fre beo\u00f0, & hie \u00fery an God\nFram \u00feam, \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6ne & on \u00feam syndon geworhte ealle \u00fea \u00feinc \u00fee gesewene syndon & ealle \u00fea \u00fee\n\u00c6rest on frym\u00fee he geworhte heofonas & eor\u00f0an & s\u00e6 & ealle \u00fea \u00feinc \u00fee on him syndon, & ealle \u00fea\n& ealle \u00fea \u00f0e of englum to deoflum forsceapene wurdon, ealle he hie of him sylfum mid his oro\u00f0e ut\n& ealle \u00fea \u00f0e \u00e6t \u00f0am r\u00e6de mid him w\u00e6ron & him \u00e6fter besawon, ealle hie wurdon of englum to\nSy\u00f0\u00f0an he geworhte of eor\u00f0an lame \u00feone \u00e6restan man \u00fee \u00e6fre w\u00e6s, \u00feone he be naman Adam nemde,\n& him ealle eor\u00f0an gesceafta on geweald sealde & s\u00e6s fixas, \u00fe\u00e6t hie him hyrsumian sceoldon.\n& he him eallum naman gesceop, \u00e6g\u00f0er ge nytenum ge fugelum ge fixum, & hie ealle gyt be \u00f0am\n& dryhten \u00e6lmihtig of Adames wynstran sidan genam \u00fe\u00e6t ribb \u00fee he \u00fe\u00e6t wif ofgeworhte \u00fee Eua hatte.\nOf \u00f0am twam \u00feurh Godes mihte is ealles middangeardes folc framcumen.\n& him God forgeaf \u00fe\u00e6t hie ealles geweald agan moston \u00fee on eor\u00f0an w\u00e6re, butan anes treowes bleda\n\u00de\u00e6t treow ys on middan neorxnawange.\nBe \u00f0am treowe Crist sylf forewarnode \u00e6g\u00f0er ge Adam ge Euan, & him s\u00e6de bam \u00fe\u00e6t swa hwylcum\n& hie eac swa dydon.\nAc \u00f0a se deofol geseah & wiste \u00fe\u00e6t him God swa mycel forgifen h\u00e6fde, & he sylf beswicen w\u00e6s & \u00fea\nGehweorrfde hine sylfne \u00fea on anre n\u00e6dran hiwe, & hie butu beswac & forl\u00e6rde.\nS\u00e6de him \u00fe\u00e6t swa hwylcum d\u00e6ge swa hie \u00fe\u00e6s treowes bleda \u00e6ton, \u00fe\u00e6t hie w\u00e6ron sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00feam gelice\nAc hit him wear\u00f0 biterlice forgolden on hyra life ge eac \u00e6fter, \u00e6g\u00f0er ge him ge eallum mancynne \u00fee\nNigon hund wintra & \u00feritig wintra Adam lifde on \u00feysse worulde on geswince & on yrm\u00fee, & sy\u00f0\u00f0an to\nMen \u00fea leofestan, us is nu for \u00fey mycel nyd\u00feearf, nu we \u00feus \u00feurh Godes mihte ealle \u00e6tg\u00e6dere syndon,\nAc utan us wendan, men \u00fea leofestan, to beterum \u00feingum, & forl\u00e6tan eallo yfolo \u00feing, & don god swa\nUs ys georne to witenne & to gehlystenne for hwylcum \u00feingum we \u00f0as gangdagas healda\u00f0 & barefote\nSe feor\u00f0a is dryhtne sylfum for his m\u00e6ran upstige of eor\u00f0an to heofonum gehalgod.\n& mid hwylcum \u00feingum we hie healdan sceolon, us is georne to witanne.\nWe hie sceolon healdan on mycelre eadmodnysse & on myclum ge\u00feylde & on so\u00f0re lufe & on eallre\nManegum haligum mannum \u00feas gangdagas syndon wi\u00f0metene, ac us is lang \u00fe\u00e6t eall to gereccanne.\nUtan \u00feeah us georne wi\u00f0 deofol scyldan eallum tidum & us ongean his yfelan lara Godes\nSe deofol d\u00e6ges & nihtes winn\u00f0 ongean us mid his geleafleste; uton we winnan ongean hine mid\nHe winn\u00f0 mid ofermodnesse; uton we ongean mid ea\u00f0modnesse.\nHe us gegearwa\u00f0 galnesse; uton we ongean cl\u00e6nnesse.\nHe gegrip\u00f0 manfulnesse; uton we ongean rihtwisnesse.\nHe us on bebringe\u00f0 yrsunge; uton we fylgean ge\u00feylde.\nHe us on asent gytsunge; uton we began mildheortnesse.\nHe us mynga\u00f0 to gifernesse; uton \u00fe\u00e6r ongean gehealdan forh\u00e6fednesse.\n& \u00e6fre ongean his yfelan willan uton wyrcan Godes willan.\nEall we sceolon efestan to Godes templum swa swi\u00f0e swa \u00f0a bion do\u00f0 to hira hyfe, to \u00feam \u00fe\u00e6t we\nWe gelyfa\u00f0, men \u00fea leofestan, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee we r\u00e6ddon on halgum bocum, \u00fe\u00e6t swa hwa swa on \u00feis \u00ferim\n& hit is eac awriten \u00fe\u00e6t nan mann hine ne sceal georwenan \u00fe\u00e6t him God miltsian nelle, \u00feeah he \u00feusend\n\u00deeah hw\u00e6\u00f0ere ne forgif\u00f0 he hie us butan we \u00fee ricenor him fram gehweorfen.\nUs syndon syndorlice on \u00f0yssum dagum forbodene, \u00feeah hie on \u00e6lcere tide forbodene syn \u00feeah swi\u00f0or\n\u00c6lcum, ge geongum ge ealdum, \u00feis f\u00e6sten is beboden \u00fe\u00e6t hie hyt sceolon healice healdan, & hyt \u00fee\nWite gehwa swa he geornor sceal Gode \u00feeowgean & healic f\u00e6stenu f\u00e6stan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee geornor deofol wile\n\u00dey we beoda\u00f0 Godes bebode & eallra his haligra, \u00fe\u00e6t nan \u00feara cristenra manna \u00fee \u00feis gehyre him\nMen \u00fea leofestan, uton gemunan \u00feone cwide \u00fe\u00e6s eadigan apostolys Petris; he cw\u00e6\u00f0: Se deoful us\nUton nu gehealdan georne \u00feis f\u00e6sten, neah \u00feam \u00fee hit awriten is on haligum bocum \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea f\u00e6ston \u00fee\nBe \u00f0am is on bocum awriten \u00fe\u00e6t God \u00feurh haligne gast hine het faran to sumere m\u00e6rre ceastre seo\nAc for \u00feam \u00fee \u00f0\u00e6t folc w\u00e6s awyrged & \u00e6breca, he him swi\u00f0e ondred & \u00fe\u00e6der faran ne dorste.\nFor \u00f0am \u00fee God w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e yrre \u00fe\u00e6re ceasterleode, \u00f0a wolde he for \u00fei Godes bebodu forfleon.\nAc him com to cy\u00f0\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t he hie forfleon ne meahte.\nHe \u00feeah on fleame w\u00e6s, o\u00f0 he to sae becwom, & him \u00fe\u00e6r scip gebohte, & mid \u00feam scipmannum him\nAc he ne mihte, swa he gemynt h\u00e6fde, Godes willan forfleon.\nAc sona swa he w\u00e6s in agan on \u00fe\u00e6t scyp, \u00fea gereste he hine on anum ende, & \u00fea sona swa \u00fea menn\n\u00dea for \u00feam \u00fea ondredon \u00fea scipmen him swi\u00f0e \u00feearle; hluton him \u00fea betwynan for hwylces hiera\n& \u00fea behluton hie hit sona to Iona, \u00feam witigan, & he his nan \u00feing nyste.\n\u00d0a wundrodon hie sona \u00fe\u00e6t se hlyt ofer \u00feone Godes \u00feegn gefeoll.\nAwrehton hine \u00fea of sl\u00e6pe & rehton hit him eall, & he \u00feafode \u00fe\u00e6t hine man wearp ut on \u00fea s\u00e6, \u00fea he\n& hine sona an mycel hw\u00e6ll forswealh, & he w\u00e6s on him \u00fery dagas & iii niht.\n& sy\u00f0\u00f0an, eal swa hit God wolde, seo s\u00e6 \u00feone fisc ferede o\u00f0 he com to \u00feam ilcan e\u00f0le \u00fee he \u00e6r on\n& he \u00f0a sona on \u00fereora daga fyrste \u00feurhfor \u00fea m\u00e6ran & \u00fea myclan burh, & bodode on \u00fe\u00e6re Godes\n& he aras of his cynesetle & him fram his cynereaf of awearp & hine mid h\u00e6ran ymbscrydde & to\n& he bebead \u00e6rest \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6g\u00f0er ge \u00fea menn ge ealle \u00fea nytenu \u00fee hie ahton sceoldon \u00fery dagas & \u00fereo\n& hie \u00f0a swa dydon, & him \u00f0a God his mildheortnesse geaf, & him fram \u00fe\u00e6t fyrene clyne adyde \u00fee\nAc hie dydon swa him to donne w\u00e6s, gecyrdon to Gode \u00e6lmihtigum, & he him sona his\nEac we r\u00e6ddon on halegum bocum \u00fe\u00e6t on sumere ceastre \u00fee w\u00e6s Uienna haten, on \u00fe\u00e6re w\u00e6s sum\nBe \u00f0am is awriten \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t folc \u00fee he bewiste wear\u00f0 \u00feearle mid f\u00e6rlicum dea\u00f0e fornumen, & swa\n\u00dea b\u00e6d se bisceop Mamertus ealle \u00fea bisceopas \u00fee on \u00f0am earde w\u00e6ron mid wependre stefne \u00fe\u00e6t hie\n& hie \u00f0a ealle swa dydon, & gesetton \u00fea him betwinan \u00fe\u00e6t man a sy\u00f0\u00f0an sceolde \u00feas \u00fery gangdagas\n& hie sona \u00e6t Gode geearnodon ece h\u00e6le & \u00fe\u00e6s f\u00e6rlican dea\u00fees afyrrednesse.\nNu we habba\u00f0 gehyred for hwi \u00feas gangdagas \u00ebrest bebodene w\u00e6ron to gehealdenne.\nGeceose nu gehwa swa hw\u00e6\u00f0er swa he wille, swa \u00fe\u00e6t betere swa \u00fe\u00e6t m\u00e6ttre.\nNe beode we nanum mannum nane niwe bebodu.\nDo gehwa swa him sylfum for Gode gebeorhlicost \u00feince, gif he hwylcum bysenum & \u00feylcum larum\nGeorne we witon \u00fe\u00e6t Gode lica\u00fe swa mycle mare swa man mare for his lufum to gode gede\u00f0, & he us\n\u00de\u00e6r is ece med, & \u00fe\u00e6r is lif butan dea\u00f0e & geogo\u00f0 butan ylde & leoht butan \u00feystrum & gefea butan",
